From 0e9d66d66cf9eb9adfe0ecd1e9c1cd7e2c9887ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Dinwoodie <adam@dinwoodie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:10:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add independent expiry and recurrence triggers

Expiry and recurrence processing currently follow gc so reports can open
the database read-only when automatic updates are disabled. This also
prevents users from expiring tasks or generating recurring instances
without allowing task IDs to be renumbered.

Add expiry and recurrence.trigger boolean settings. Unset or blank values
inherit the effective gc setting, preserving existing behavior. Explicit
values control each operation independently, while recurrence=0 remains
the master switch for recurrence processing and template retirement.

Use the same fallback logic for dispatch and database access so enabled
maintenance can persist changes with gc=0 without compacting IDs. Document
the options and cover inheritance, overrides, independent operation, stable
IDs, template retirement, and read-only access.

Validation: build succeeded; all eight targeted CTest suites passed with
libfaketime available. clang-format, Black, and git diff --check passed.

Fixes #4216

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
